From 4b397325943e70d3dbaaff63b5f622ab48668d62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qinyibo <54056901+Qinyibo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:57:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm: retain dead-panel recovery until a matching successful
 modeset

Do not clear the panel rail-recovery flag before touch PREPARE can fail.
Use the existing panel lock and fault/recovery sequence snapshots so an old
success cannot clear a newer ESD/enable failure. Preserve ordinary gesture
rail retention and OFF/LP notify-only policy; retain notification coalescing.

Extracted production-function regression: old 13/29 failures, candidate
35/35 checks pass with UBSan and threaded event interleavings. Full Image,
unchanged config/Module.symvers, boot payload invariants, partition readback
and one normal system boot pass. No wake stress or fault injection.
Intermittent INIT=0x9D root cause and real recovery remain unproven.
